---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icons from "../components/Icons.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Beijing Subway to Attractions: Complete Guide [2026]" description="Navigate Beijing by subway to every major attraction. Station names in Chinese, exit numbers, walking directions, fares, and tips for first-time riders.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12 pb-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-base-900 mb-3">Beijing Subway Guide for Attractions</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-base-500 leading-relaxed mb-8">Every major Beijing attraction, with its nearest subway station, exit, and walking directions. Navigate like a local.</p>
  </div>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-16">
    <div class="border border-base-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-base-100 text-base-500 uppercase text-xs tracking-wider">
          <tr><th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-left">Attraction</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-left">Subway Station</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-left">Line</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-left">Exit</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-base-100"><td class="px-4 py-3"><a href="/attractions/forbidden-city/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">Forbidden City</a></td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Tiananmen East</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Line 1</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">B</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-base-100"><td class="px-4 py-3"><a href="/attractions/temple-of-heaven/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">Temple of Heaven</a></td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Tiantan Dongmen</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Line 5</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">A</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-base-100"><td class="px-4 py-3"><a href="/attractions/summer-palace/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">Summer Palace</a></td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Beigongmen</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Line 4</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">D</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-base-100"><td class="px-4 py-3"><a href="/attractions/tiananmen-square/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">Tiananmen Square</a></td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Tiananmen East</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Line 1</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">A</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-base-100"><td class="px-4 py-3"><a href="/attractions/lama-temple/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">Lama Temple</a></td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Yonghegong</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Line 2 / 5</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">C</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-base-100"><td class="px-4 py-3"><a href="/attractions/national-museum/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">National Museum</a></td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Tiananmen East</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Line 1</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">C</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-base-100"><td class="px-4 py-3"><a href="/attractions/jingshan-park/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">Jingshan Park</a></td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Nanluoguxiang</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Line 6 / 8</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">E</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3"><a href="/attractions/nanluoguxiang/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">Nanluoguxiang</a></td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Nanluoguxiang</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">Line 6 / 8</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-base-600">E</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-16 border-t border-base-200 pt-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Subway Tips</h2>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">How to Ride the Beijing Subway</h2>
    <ol class="space-y-4 text-sm text-base-600 list-decimal pl-5 mb-8">
      <li class="pl-1"><strong>Get a Yikatong card</strong> \u2014 Buy one at the service counter inside any subway station for a CNY 20 deposit. Load it with credit (CNY 50 is plenty for a week). Tap in and out at the gates. The card works on all subway lines and most city buses. Refund the deposit at major stations (Tiananmen East, Dongzhimen, Xidan) on your last day.</li>
      <li class="pl-1"><strong>Pass through security</strong> \u2014 Every station has X-ray scanners at every entrance. Place your bag on the belt and walk through the metal detector. The process takes 30 seconds to 2 minutes depending on the queue. Allow extra time during rush hour (7:30\u20139am and 5:30\u20137pm).</li>
      <li class="pl-1"><strong>Find your line and direction</strong> \u2014 All signage is in Chinese and English. Look for the line number (colored circle) and the direction (listed as the terminal station). Maps above the platform doors show every stop on the line.</li>
      <li class="pl-1"><strong>Pay attention to exits</strong> \u2014 Most central stations have 4\u20138 exits labeled A, B, C, D (sometimes with numbers like B1, B2). Check the exit map near the ticket gates before you leave the station. Taking the wrong exit can put you on the wrong side of a 10-lane road with no pedestrian crossing.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Fares and Payment</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-base-600 mb-8">
      <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><Icons name="check" size={16} class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><span><strong>Yikatong card:</strong> CNY 3 for trips under 6km, capping at CNY 9 for long journeys. The card automatically calculates the fare when you tap out. Monthly pass options exist for stays longer than 2 weeks.</span></li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><Icons name="check" size={16} class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><span><strong>Mobile payment:</strong> Alipay and WeChat Pay both support subway QR code entry. Set this up before your trip if possible \u2014 it means one less card to carry.</span></li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><Icons name="check" size={16} class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><span><strong>Single-journey tickets:</strong> Available from ticket machines (English mode available). You\u2019ll need small bills or coins. Not recommended for multiple rides \u2014 the Yikatong card is much faster.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Tips for a Smooth Ride</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-base-600">
      <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><Icons name="check" size={16} class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><span>Subway operates <strong>5am to 11pm</strong> daily. Last trains depart around 10:30pm from most stations \u2014 don\u2019t push it too close or you\u2019ll be taking a taxi.</span></li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><Icons name="check" size={16} class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><span>All stations have <strong>English signage and announcements</strong>. Station names are announced in both Mandarin and English before each stop.</span></li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><Icons name="check" size={16} class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><span><strong>Avoid rush hour</strong> (7:30\u20139am and 5:30\u20137pm) if possible \u2014 Line 1 and Line 10 can be shoulder-to-shoulder. If you must travel during rush hour, position yourself near the doors and be ready to exit quickly.</span></li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><Icons name="check" size={16} class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><span><strong>Download a subway map</strong> to your phone before arriving. The official Beijing Subway app has an English mode, or save a screenshot of the network map. Cell service works in most underground stations but not all tunnel sections.</span></li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><Icons name="check" size={16} class="text-accent mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><span><strong>Transfers are free</strong> \u2014 you only pay once per journey regardless of how many lines you change. Follow the transfer signs (marked with the destination line\u2019s color). Major transfer stations like Dongzhimen and Xidan can involve 5\u201310 minute walks between platforms.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
